-- title:
--   A prime Hecke element at ℓ, supported at ℓ
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb Q$ and let $q'$ be a prime such that the quaternion algebra $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ satisfies [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b q'`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_EichlerOrder.html#L87), that is: $a<0$, $b<0$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ the completed algebra $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ has all its nonzero elements invertible exactly when $q'$ lies in $v$. Let $R$ be a $\mathbb Z$-submodule of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ and $N\in\mathbb N$ with [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsEichlerOrder R N`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_EichlerOrder.html#L69), i.e. $R=\Lambda_1\sqcap\Lambda_2$ for two maximal orders $\Lambda_1,\Lambda_2$ (orders maximal among the orders containing them), the relative index of $R$ in $\Lambda_1$ as additive subgroups being $N$. Let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell\neq q'$ and $\ell\nmid N$. Then there exists a unit $s$ of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb A_{\mathbb Q}^{\mathrm{fin}}$ such that: (i) for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ not containing $\ell$, the component [`Submodule.finiteAdeleEvalAt`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L36) of $s$ at $v$ equals $1$; (ii) $s$ lies in [`QuaternionAlgebra.primeHeckeSet R ℓ`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_ClassSetHecke.html#L109), that is, $s$ lies in the finite adelic box of $R$ (the additive subgroup generated by the elements $z\otimes\alpha$ with $z\in R$ and $\alpha$ an everywhere integral finite adele), $\ell\cdot s^{-1}$ lies in that box, while neither $s^{-1}$ nor $\ell^{-1}s$ does; and (iii) [`CerednikDrinfeld.meetOrder R s`](def/CerednikDrinfeld_ClassSetGraph.html#L15), namely $R\sqcap$ [`Submodule.conjByFiniteIdele R s`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L31) (the elements of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ whose image under `includeLeft` lies in $s\cdot(\text{box of }R)\cdot s^{-1}$), is an Eichler order in the above sense of level $N\ell$.
--
--   This is the adelic construction of a Hecke element at a prime $\ell$ unramified for the quaternion algebra and coprime to the Eichler level: a double-coset representative $\hat R^\times\,\mathrm{diag}(\ell,1)\,\hat R^\times$ concentrated at $\ell$, whose associated intersection order has level $N\ell$. It supplies the edges issuing from a vertex in the Čerednik–Drinfeld class-set graph, and is used in the finiteness and orbit statement [`CerednikDrinfeld.evenAwayUnits_finite_stabilizer_vertex_and_exists_finset_orbits_of_not_dvd`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.evenAwayUnits_finite_stabilizer_vertex_and_exists_finset_orbits_of_not_dvd).
-- source:
